Chapter: OverApply

 The Rulebook's third application case (DevelopersRulebook.md:260):
 over-applying a NAMED definition, where the extra arguments apply to what
 the definition RETURNS. `partial.codex` cannot reach it -- its only
 definition, add3, returns an Integer -- so this file exists to carry the
 shape that needs a definition returning a function.

 `choose` has two return paths and no recursion, so what these lines vary
 is how the RESULT is applied and not what the definition is.

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (a) (b) (c) = a + b + c

  choose : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  choose (n) = if n == 0 then add3 1 else add3 2

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("control-flat: " & show (add3 1 2 3))
   let c = choose 0
   in print-line-uni ("stepwise: " & show ((c 2) 3))
   print-line-uni ("named-over: " & show (choose 0 2 3))
   print-line-uni ("named-over-alt: " & show (choose 1 2 3))
   print-line-uni ("after: " & show (add3 4 5 6))
  end
